# src/apps/daemon/internal/runtime/warp

## Purpose
WireGuard/WARP scanning, configuration, and runtime support used by proxy/API flows.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `runtime` (rank 4; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (8): `noise.go`, `warp.go`, `warp_account.go`, `warp_account_test.go`, `warp_export_test.go`, `warp_handshake.go`, `warp_scanner.go`, `warp_scanner_test.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `warp`.
- Notable exported surface: `CloudflareWarpPublicKey`, `EndpointResult`, `GenerateHiddifyConfig`, `GenerateSingBoxWireGuardConfig`, `GenerateV2RayWireGuardURL`, `GenerateWireGuardConfig`, `GenerateWireGuardKeyPair`, `IcmpPing`, `InjectNoise`, `NewWarpAccountClient` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/remoteaction`.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/adapters/mobilebind`.

## Invariants
- `runtime` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

